From: Juraj Oršulić <juraj.orsulic@fer.hr>
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: defer NVPCF notifications only in fine-grained mode

RmDeferNvpcfNotifyIfIdle(), added by NVIDIA PR #1299, takes the dynamic
power mutex unconditionally. os_ref_dynamic_power(nv, NV_DYNAMIC_PM_FINE),
which it replaces on that path, returns without locking when the
configured mode is coarse or NV_DYNAMIC_PM_NEVER, and
rm_init_dynamic_power_management() selects NV_DYNAMIC_PM_NEVER when
creating the mutex fails, leaving it NULL. An NVPCF notification would
then dereference NULL, and in coarse mode notifications would be
deferred although the GPU is not resumed for them.

Return NV_FALSE in both modes, so the original path handles them.

---
diff --git a/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/dynamic-power.c b/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/dynamic-power.c
index c999c92..6056485 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/dynamic-power.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/dynamic-power.c
@@ -1532,7 +1532,14 @@ NvBool RmDeferNvpcfNotifyIfIdle(
     nv_priv_t *nvp = NV_GET_NV_PRIV(nv);
     NvBool bDefer;
 
-    if (nvp == NULL)
+    /*
+     * Defer only where os_ref_dynamic_power(nv, NV_DYNAMIC_PM_FINE) would
+     * take the mutex and could resume the GPU. In coarse mode it returns
+     * without doing either, and in NV_DYNAMIC_PM_NEVER the mutex may not
+     * exist: rm_init_dynamic_power_management() selects that mode when creating
+     * the mutex fails.
+     */
+    if ((nvp == NULL) || (NV_DYNAMIC_PM_FINE > nvp->dynamic_power.mode))
     {
         return NV_FALSE;
     }
